.TH XANARA 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xanara \- read, annotate and edit PDF documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xanara
[\fB\-\-page=\fIN\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B xanara
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Xanara
is the document viewer and PDF editor of the Selviana Desktop Environment,
written from scratch by the DebION Dev-Team on poppler and cairo.
.PP
One window holds several documents in tabs, next to a
.B Home
tab with quick actions (open, merge, images to PDF) and the recent documents
as thumbnails. Tabs are reordered by dragging and closed with their x or the
middle mouse button.
.PP
The toolbar holds the side panel switch, the pointer (select or hand), the
zoom and the editing modes
.BR Annotate ,
.BR Edit ,
.BR Page ,
.BR Form ,
.BR Fill ,
.BR Convert ,
.B Protect
and
.BR Tools ,
followed by undo, redo, export and the properties panel. The context toolbar
below shows the tools of the active mode. On narrow or scaled windows modes
and tools that do not fit move into overflow menus. Tools that need a program
that is not installed are shown greyed; their tooltip names the Debian
package to install.
.PP
The icon rail on the left switches the side panel between search results,
page thumbnails (drag a thumbnail to move the page), the outline, bookmarks,
the list of annotations and saved signatures; its bottom shows the current
page and the page count. The properties panel on the right sets colour,
opacity, line width, font size and alignment of the armed tool or the
selected annotation, and shows the document information otherwise.
.PP
Pages are rendered at the exact resolution of the screen (zoom times the SDE
interface scale) in 512 pixel tiles on a background thread, and kept in a
memory bounded cache.
.SS Modes
.TP
.B Annotate
Highlight, underline, squiggly and strike-out; text boxes and sticky notes;
pen and eraser; rectangle, ellipse, arrow and line; measuring distances;
rubber stamps (Approved, Draft, Confidential, ...); signatures (drawn or from
an image); showing or hiding all annotations.
.TP
.B Edit
Text and images placed on the page; links to web addresses or pages,
watermarks, background colours, headers and footers, Bates numbers and
cropping (these use
.BR qpdf (1)).
.TP
.B Page
Insert, extract, split, append, rotate, delete and move pages and print page
numbers (qpdf).
.TP
.B Form
Add text fields, check boxes, radio buttons, combo and list boxes, push
buttons and signature fields (qpdf); highlight the fields. Fields are filled
in by clicking them.
.TP
.B Fill
Type text anywhere, check marks, crosses, dots, today's date, initials and
signatures.
.TP
.B Convert
Export pages as PNG or JPEG images, the text as plain text, HTML or Markdown;
make a PDF from images; merge PDFs (qpdf).
.TP
.B Protect
Save a copy protected with a password (AES-256) and permissions; remove a
password; mark areas for redaction and apply them: pages with marks are
replaced by an image of themselves with the areas painted black, so nothing
under the boxes survives; remove the metadata (qpdf).
.TP
.B Tools
Compress (ghostscript when installed, otherwise qpdf), OCR into a searchable
PDF (
.BR tesseract (1)
and qpdf), compare with another PDF side by side, print with
.BR lp (1).
.PP
Changes to the structure of the PDF are made on a working copy; nothing is
written to the original until it is saved. Saving writes a complete new file
next to the original and renames it over the original only after it was
written and read back successfully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page= N
Open the first
.I FILE
at page
.I N
(1 is the first page).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and the poppler version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.PP
Every
.I FILE
opens in a tab of its own and may also be a file:// URI. Without files the
tabs of the last session are restored.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q
Open, save, save a copy, print, close the tab, quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab, Ctrl+Page Down, Ctrl+Page Up
Next and previous tab (Home included).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+1 ... Ctrl+Alt+8
Switch to the Annotate ... Tools mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Enter, Shift+Enter, F3
Search, next and previous result.
.TP
.B Ctrl+wheel, Ctrl++, Ctrl+\-, Ctrl+0, Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2
Zoom, 100\ %, fit page, fit width.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R, Ctrl+Shift+R
Rotate the view.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L, Ctrl+D
Go to a page number; bookmark the page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Cycle normal, night and sepia reading.
.TP
.B F5, F9, F10, F11
Presentation, side panel, properties panel, full screen.
.TP
.B V H U Q K N T P E R O A L M G
Select, highlight, underline, squiggly, strike out, sticky note, text box,
pen, eraser, rectangle, ellipse, arrow, line, measure, signature.
.TP
.B Delete, Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z, Esc
Delete the selected annotation, undo, redo, leave the current tool.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
The
.B [xanara]
section keeps the layout, reading mode, mode, side panel, properties panel,
initials,
.B restore_session
(default true) and
.B cache_mb
(rendered tile cache in MiB, default 224).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/xanara\-history
Recent documents and the last page and zoom of each.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/xanara\-session
The tabs of the last session.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/xanara\-bookmarks
Bookmarked pages.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sde/xanara/signatures/
Saved signatures (PNG).
.SH NOTES
With poppler older than the release that can create FreeText and Ink
annotations natively, text boxes, drawings, arrows and fill-in marks are
stored as image stamps that look the same in every PDF viewer.
.SH SEE ALSO
